00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:11,400
- [Mike] No, just old.

248
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:14,200
- You've been going together
for a year and a half.

249
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,267
last month you finally
became engaged.

250
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:18,133
I'm just not like that.

251
00:09:18,133 --> 00:09:19,633
- [Tom Servo] I'm easy. Hehe.

252
00:09:19,633 --> 00:09:22,367
- That's fine. But, are you
sure you'll always be in love

253
00:09:22,367 --> 00:09:23,600
like you are now?

254
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:25,100
- [Tom Servo] With
somebody, sure.

255
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:28,500
- Liz, how can you
say such a thing?

256
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,100
- Oh, wait a minute, Peg,
please don't get upset.

257
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:35,967
All I mean is, are you
sure you see eye to eye

258
00:09:35,967 --> 00:09:37,167
about things like...

259
00:09:37,167 --> 00:09:38,333
- [Tom Servo] The trade deficit.

260
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:40,700
- Well, like,
money and children?

261
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,633
- [Tom Servo] Bogus.

262
00:09:41,633 --> 00:09:43,167
- What's right and what's wrong.

263
00:09:44,567 --> 00:09:46,900
How do you get along with
each other's families?

264
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,033
- [Mike] Boring.

265
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:49,667
- Suppose your
parents won't approve.

266
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:52,967
You have to think
about these things Peg.

267
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,600
- [Crow] Look, can
we get separate beds?

268
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,100
- As far as I'm concerned,

269
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:58,433
you don't have to think if
you've found the right man.

270
00:09:58,433 --> 00:10:00,900
- [Tom Servo] Excuse me,
but that's my boyfriend.

271
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:04,800
- You better go and
send that telegram.

272
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,267
- [Mike] I'm too much in
love to send a telegram.

273
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:09,567
- [Crow] I love his picture.

274
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,200
Maybe someday I'll
meet him in person.

275
00:10:14,533 --> 00:10:16,133
- [Tom Servo] Let's
see if my, yeah.

276
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:20,367
If my, if my demands are not
met the screens of those who've

277
00:10:20,367 --> 00:10:23,067
wronged me in the smell of
burning flesh will fill the

278
00:10:23,067 --> 00:10:26,233
student, union.

279
00:10:26,233 --> 00:10:27,533
- How's the essay coming?

280
00:10:27,533 --> 00:10:28,500
- [Mike] Not so good mom.

281
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,833
- Page two? Not so good.

282
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,300
- [Crow] Will you just lay off.

283
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,367
- I can do an engineering
paper in two days Liz.

284
00:10:34,367 --> 00:10:37,533
I've been working on
this english assignment
for a week and

285
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:38,367
nothing.

286
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:39,833
- Gosh, Andy,

287
00:10:39,833 --> 00:10:41,433
you got to get your English
or you won't graduate.

288
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,300
- [Crow] Would you
just leave me alone.

289
00:10:44,767 --> 00:10:47,167
- Look, why don't we meet
at the library tonight?

290
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:48,433
- [Crow] Oh yeah.

291
00:10:48,433 --> 00:10:49,667
- Maybe I can help.

292
00:10:49,667 --> 00:10:51,433
- Gee, thanks Liz,
that'd be swell of you.

293
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,167
- [Mike] Conforms
without a cause.

294
00:10:53,167 --> 00:10:55,967
- Hey look, the
lovebirds have arrived.

295
00:10:55,967 --> 00:10:57,067
- [Crow] And they're
leaving their droppings

296
00:10:57,067 --> 00:10:58,400
all over the place. Hehe.

297
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,400
- Nothing like advertising.

298
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,833
- They got engaged last night.

299
00:11:01,833 --> 00:11:03,333
(dramatic gasping)

300
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:05,800
- Peggy said they're getting
married right after commence.

301
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,800
- Marriage?

302
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,133
- [Tom Servo] It's immoral.

303
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:13,000
- Boy, Peggy thinks
it's all handholding

304
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,500
and gazing into
each other's eyes.

305
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,300
- [Mike] She doesn't know
about the stench of ammonia

306
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,967
from the piles of
crap filled diapers.

307
00:11:17,967 --> 00:11:19,400
- You were like that once too.

308
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,867
- [Crow] And now, a firm
and hardy hand clap.

309
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:23,100
- Those first dates
were exciting.

310
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:24,033
The more I got to know you,

311
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:25,700
the more I liked what I knew.

312
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,800
Though, I suppose I was
really intrigued by the

313
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,267
things I didn't know about you.

314
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:30,533
- [Tom Servo] Like you
being a communist and all.

315
00:11:30,533 --> 00:11:33,367
- we seem to have lots
in common, didn't we?

316
00:11:33,367 --> 00:11:35,333
There was so many things
we could do together.

317
00:11:35,333 --> 00:11:36,833
- [Mike] What the
hell was that for?

318
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:39,467
You were supposed to cover
down a line. I told you.

319
00:11:39,467 --> 00:11:40,667
Come here, look at that.

320
00:11:40,667 --> 00:11:41,900
- I wish I could
argue with you there.

321
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:43,367
- [Crow] But you've
emasculated me.

322
00:11:43,367 --> 00:11:45,500
- You really enjoy a
good argument, don't you?

323
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,900
I haven't forgotten the time
the Dean's rule on drinking

324
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:49,133
came out.

325
00:11:49,133 --> 00:11:50,667
- [Tom Servo] I can
quit anytime I want to.

326
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:53,033
- That was the day I found out
we could argue like anything

327
00:11:53,033 --> 00:11:54,667
and somehow love
each other more.

328
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:58,533
I thought expulsion was
too stiff a penalty,

329
00:11:58,533 --> 00:12:01,267
one small slip and some guy's
whole life could be changed.

330
00:12:01,267 --> 00:12:03,333
- [Mike] Drinking in college?
I never heard of that.

331
00:12:03,333 --> 00:12:06,200
- Andy, but I couldn't
entirely agree.

332
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,033
Expelling somebody is a
serious thing of course, but,

333
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:11,567
so is drinking in a dorm.

334
00:12:11,567 --> 00:12:13,567
All those people living
so close together.

335
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,533
- [Crow] Look would you just
lay off for ten seconds.

336
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:16,633
- Well we didn't
settle the issue,

337
00:12:16,633 --> 00:12:18,167
but it sure was fun trying.

338
00:12:19,567 --> 00:12:21,967
I wanted to convince you
and you try to convince me.

339
00:12:21,967 --> 00:12:25,300
I guess we became most
convinced about each other.

340
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,833
- We must have,

341
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:29,567
up until a month ago, that
finger look kind of bare.

342
00:12:29,567 --> 00:12:30,667
You remember?

343
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:31,667
- [Tom Servo] Naked.

344
00:12:34,933 --> 00:12:37,433
- [Crow] Zirconia, that jerk.

345
00:12:37,433 --> 00:12:39,900
- [Mike] QVC. Thank you.

346
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:42,433
- [Tom Servo] Uh, I figured
if like we split it,

347
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:44,700
the cost, we can afford it.

348
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,400
- [Crow] Gifts, given in
dorms, punished by expulsion.

349
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,533
- [Tom Servo] ] Hmm, you
tastes like Jean Kirkpatrick.

350
00:12:55,533 --> 00:12:58,533
- [Mike] Oh I'm on fire,
enough. That's enough.

351
00:12:58,533 --> 00:13:00,167
- [Crow] Honey, I also
got you a subscription to

352
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:01,833
modern maturity.

353
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:04,567
- Gosh, I think our folks
were even more excited

354
00:13:04,567 --> 00:13:06,067
than we were.

355
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,333
- [Mike] Yeah, when your
dad got the shotgun down.

356
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,567
- Ready to go back to the dorm?

357
00:13:08,567 --> 00:13:09,400
- Hi.

358
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,900
- Hi.

359
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,667
- Hey, congratulations you
too. I just heard the news.

360
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,167
- Oh thanks Andy.

361
00:13:14,167 --> 00:13:16,667
(funky music)

362
00:13:21,733 --> 00:13:23,233
- Have you found a place
to live around here?

363
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:25,067
- Oh, I don't think we
have to worry about it.

364
00:13:25,067 --> 00:13:26,800
Can we just find a little
apartment somewhere.

365
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:27,833
- Peggy.

366
00:13:27,833 --> 00:13:29,500
- [Crow] It's the heat, run.

367
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,567
- Hi darling.

368
00:13:31,567 --> 00:13:32,667
- [Mike] Oh poopey.

369
00:13:32,667 --> 00:13:33,600
- What are you doing here?

370
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,267
- We've got your telegram.

371
00:13:35,267 --> 00:13:36,767
- Aren't you thrilled?

372
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:38,200
- Should we be?

373
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,800
- Now don't be crossed Betty.
Let's hear Peggy's side.

374
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,033
- [Mike] Well, he's
good in the sack and

375
00:13:42,033 --> 00:13:43,200
he likes to get high.

376
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:48,367
- Well, we've been going steady
for over three months now.

377
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:51,433
Mother, dad, we have such
a wonderful time together.

378
00:13:51,433 --> 00:13:52,700
- [Tom Servo] Oh my god.

379
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:54,800
- I'm in love, really in
love for the first time.

380
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,200
we planned to marry
right after commencement,

381
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,667
it's as simple as that.

382
00:13:58,667 --> 00:13:59,967
- [Crow] You're grounded.

383
00:13:59,967 --> 00:14:01,267
- Peggy, you wrote us
last week that Joe was

384
00:14:01,267 --> 00:14:03,033
going into
professional football,

385
00:14:03,033 --> 00:14:04,633
has he signed on
with any team yet?

386
00:14:04,633 --> 00:14:07,267
- Well, no, he hasn't
got a contract yet,

387
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:10,467
but he's been told he's a very
good chance of getting one,

388
00:14:10,467 --> 00:14:13,000
after all, he's been the star
of our team here this year,

389
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,267
you know?

390
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:15,533
- Peg, your mother and
I have come down here

391
00:14:15,533 --> 00:14:17,233
to ask you to put
off your wedding.

392
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:18,467
- [Tom Servo] And to kill Joe.

393
00:14:18,467 --> 00:14:20,300
- At least after
you've graduated.

394
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,800
Now, dear, if you'll wait,

395
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,767
we can help you get a house
and you can set up a home

396
00:14:23,767 --> 00:14:24,600
properly.

397
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,900
- [Crow] Take the house.

398
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:26,800
- [Mike And Tom
Servo] Take the house.

399
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,433
- Dad, I love Joe.

400
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:29,933
- [Tom Servo] Kill
us, please kill us.

401
00:14:29,933 --> 00:14:32,200
- We can live in
a little apartment
wherever we're situated.

402
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,667
Being with Joe means more
to me than anything else.

403
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:36,000
And we won't wait.

404
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,233
- But dear,

405
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:39,967
You only have one year
and a month more to go.

406
00:14:39,967 --> 00:14:42,333
It be such a pity
not to finish here.

407
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:43,633
- [Mike] Captain Spalding.

408
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:44,700
- And while your
finishing last year,

409
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:46,033
Joe can get established
in football.

410
00:14:46,033 --> 00:14:48,100
If that's what he really wants.

411
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:50,333
And you'll have some more time
to see if you're right for

412
00:14:50,333 --> 00:14:51,500
each other.

413
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,533
- That theoretical
stuff, gives me a pain.

414
00:14:53,533 --> 00:14:55,967
We're sure now we're
right for each other.

415
00:14:55,967 --> 00:14:58,633
And that's all that's
really important.

416
00:14:58,633 --> 00:15:00,367
- Peggy, we want to meet Joe.

417
00:15:00,367 --> 00:15:01,567
Now look,

418
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,033
- [Tom Servo] Don't dear.

419
00:15:03,033 --> 00:15:04,600
- Why don't we all have
dinner together at the hotel

420
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,100
tonight?

421
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:08,633
And then he can tell us all
about this football business.

422
00:15:08,633 --> 00:15:10,667
- Football is Joe's
profession, mother,

423
00:15:10,667 --> 00:15:12,733
and it's just as good
as anything else.

424
00:15:12,733 --> 00:15:13,867
- [Crow] Get a rope, honey.

425
00:15:13,867 --> 00:15:15,400
- Joe and I had already
made plans for a

426
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,400
date tonight and I see no
reason to change them now.

427
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,633
- But Peggy Dear-

428
00:15:18,633 --> 00:15:20,600
- Your not going to
stop us marrying.

429
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,433
Dad thinks all we have to do
is pay for something and he'll

430
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:23,367
get his own way.

431
00:15:23,367 --> 00:15:24,500
- [Tom Servo] Worked till now.

432
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:25,733
- You think by treating
me like a child,

433
00:15:25,733 --> 00:15:27,500
you can force me to
do what you want.

434
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:28,933
You're both wrong.

435
00:15:28,933 --> 00:15:31,333
I'm no child, I'm me
and I'll do what I want.

436
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:34,567
- [Mike] Well honey, it looks
likely spawned a demon seed.

437
00:15:36,933 --> 00:15:38,167
- Don't worry, Betty.

438
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:40,133
She'll get over it. Just
a touch of hysterics,

439
00:15:40,133 --> 00:15:43,067
that's all, why by the time
the end of the semester comes,

440
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:45,700
she'll probably be madly
in love with someone else.

441
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:47,533
Come on. We will see her
again in the morning.

442
00:15:47,533 --> 00:15:49,667
- [Crow] Let's hit the
bar it's happy hour.

443
00:15:51,133 --> 00:15:52,933
- [Tom Servo] Young
Colonel Sanders.

444
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,100
- [Mike] There's
no football player.

445
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:57,633
It might be in
the swing fighter.

446
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:02,100
- Oh Joe, I'm so mixed
up about everything.

447
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,567
- [Crow] Original
or extra crispy?

448
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:04,933
- Folks trying to stop us.

449
00:16:06,067 --> 00:16:07,700
They've always tried
to run my life.

450
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:09,233
- [Mike] I want
you to run my life.

451
00:16:09,233 --> 00:16:12,567
- Like when I wanted to go
to a dance at a Roadhouse.

452
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:14,400
Dad insisted that
I stay at home.

453
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:15,567
- [Mike] Just cause
Patrick Swayze was there.

454
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:17,900
- I was so mad, I
climbed out of a window

455
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,433
and went to a
girlfriend's house.

456
00:16:19,433 --> 00:16:20,500
- [Mike] That's
kind of odd, honey.

457
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:22,700
- And my folks were frantic.

458
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:24,867
They looked all over from me.

459
00:16:24,867 --> 00:16:26,167
Even called the police.

460
00:16:26,167 --> 00:16:28,200
- [Crow] Finally found
me at that crack house.

461
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,600
- What a girl.

462
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:33,167
I had so many brothers and
sisters, nobody to miss me,

463
00:16:33,167 --> 00:16:34,367
if I left them.

464
00:16:34,367 --> 00:16:35,900
- [Tom Servo] Oh
who cares about you?

465
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,700
- Take a couple of days for
anyone to realize I'd gone.

466
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:41,467
- And believe me being an only
child has its disadvantages.

467
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:44,700
(making honing noises)

468
00:16:46,633 --> 00:16:48,267
- In college has
been sheer heaven.

469
00:16:48,267 --> 00:16:49,633
- [Mike] except for the classes.

470
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,833
- Joe we've got to do something.

471
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:52,533
They'll do anything
to break us up.

472
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:56,967
I wish I hadn't sent that
telegram, if Liz hadn't made me.

473
00:16:59,367 --> 00:17:00,700
- Look honey.

474
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:01,367
- [Tom Servo] I should
tell you. I'm a woman.

475
00:17:01,367 --> 00:17:02,600
- I love you.

476
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:03,867
I want to marry you.

477
00:17:03,867 --> 00:17:04,767
- [Tom Servo] But
what is this crap?

478
00:17:04,767 --> 00:17:06,167
- I love you too Joe.

479
00:17:06,167 --> 00:17:08,067
I don't ever want
to be away from you.

480
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:10,800
- [Crow] We have a winner.

481
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:13,533
- [Tom Servo] Luminary
returns indicate love.

482
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:15,300
- [Mike] He's at the 40, the 50.

483
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,200
He might go all the way.

484
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,433
- [Crow] You tastes
like Troy Donahue.

485
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:20,533
- [Tom servo] You taste
like Eleanor Donahue.

486
00:17:20,533 --> 00:17:22,733
- [Mike] Oh, I'm spent,
it was incredible.

487
00:17:23,767 --> 00:17:25,133
- We'll work something out.

488
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,933
- [Tom Servo] Watch
out for snakes.

489
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,333
- [Crow] Meanwhile,

490
00:17:32,333 --> 00:17:34,233
back in the cold bitter
Loveless life of her parents.

491
00:17:34,233 --> 00:17:35,733
- Well, good morning Liz.

492
